;; PROBLEM SELECTION — m93J02. Verified by elaboration, not metadata: exits 0
;; with one `declaration uses `sorry`` diagnostic. Richest write-up in the
;; non-a-family open pool (13,157 B).
;;
;; THE DELIBERATE CONTRAST WITH f9, AND ITS CONFOUND, STATED PLAINLY.
;; f9's a01J06 touches an @why-edged pattern, so the cascade's :why-hop route
;; can fire. m93J02 touches none, so on this problem the cascade can only
;; produce :leaf and :co-incidence offers. That is the contrast worth having:
;; it makes f9's cascade prediction falsifiable against a case where the
;; mechanism is structurally unable to contribute.
;;
;; It is NOT a controlled comparison, and must not be reported as one. f9 and
;; f10 differ in BOTH family (a vs m) and edgedness, because only 5 of the 207
;; open problems touch an edged pattern and ALL FIVE are a-family — family
;; distance and cascade reach cannot both be had. Any f9/f10 difference is
;; therefore not attributable to either factor alone. The honest reading is
;; per-frame predictions, not a between-frame effect.
;;
;; Family distance from f9 satisfies frame-2's cross-problem recall-leakage
;; criterion, which f9 itself departs from.
;;
;; ANALYST HANDOFF: unchanged from f9 — apm/conductor.clj `close!` bells the
;; :analyst-seat exactly once after a terminal close, never mid-frame
;; (futon3c b27bccf7).

